phase P0
title Reconcile the design and the prototype
description
    Class: not readily verifiable.
    Kind: verification-suite.
    Goal: one source of truth before any Plan is written: the prototype and its suite brought up
    to the design's newest decisions (OD28 to OD31), and the design brought up to the prototype's
    newer decisions (convergence D1 to D222, round 13's API changes, FOR-ARPIT's accepted calls),
    recorded as OD46 to OD51.
    Verified by: prototype suite cases derived from the design's text, each seen failing first;
    the old suite's gates (lock, falsify, lies, mutants, searches, graph gate, type tests,
    front-check, CLI pins, Story checks); the stage A close-out review, area by area.
    One iteration: one area: implement it in the prototype or record it in the design, run the
    suite, review.
    Exit criteria: every design decision has passing prototype cases; every prototype decision is
    in the design or listed as a conflict for the user; no disagreement left; gates pass.
    False pass: cases bent to fit the code. Caught by: expected results derived from the design.
    Gates: the old suite's falsify parts, which reject null, broken, tampered and lying runtimes
    (`packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/conformance/falsify.ts`).
    Budget: the Epic's Budget section, row P0 to P2 (spent: 8 rounds allowed).
    Failure limit: 2.
    Stops: a guarantee change; a conflict only the user can decide. User's read: each area's
    reconciliation (now notes).
    Prototype: yes.
    Draws from: skill:policy-convergence when reviews repeat a root cause; skill:policy-testing for
    the suite; skill:review at each checkpoint.
